  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/aee2e080-8db5-4749-8db4-777a394138b6-image.png\" style=\"width: 70px; height: 144px;\" /></p><p>According to the information given in the question, the part of the chain that envelopes the pulley is very small. Therefore, the acceleration of the chain can be written as,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></mfrac><mi>g</mi></math></p><p>Since&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></mfrac><mi>g</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>L</mi></mfrac><mi>g</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mi>x</mi></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p></blockquote>",
